{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"justjack420","id":"592252026226999306","is_bot":0,"username":"justjack420"},"author_id":"592252026226999306","channel_id":"746818810954121236","content":"Could be a shadow person that extends and moves through it or \"swap places\" with it.","created_at":"2021-03-10T03:59:03.789000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"819056738468626434","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"746818810954121236","content":"i mean the good news is the echo isnt a creature (it has some wild rule implications, like eldrich blast cant target an echo), so an echo cant host an EK, and due to how i wrote living shadow (specifically because of teleport like powers, tho i didnt think of what happens if a host teleports.... as a ruling id say it follows the 'if the host is dead or doesnt cast a shadow' rule) they should manifest if they teleport swap with their echo... it would likely be a really rough class to play, with massive nerfs.... basically for a race that has 0 mobility, and takes damage when in a form with mobility, mobility classes are likely a really bad choice.\n\nEK, Shadow Monk (to some degree all monks), druids wouldnt really feel good with flying forms, Cavalier (you cant ride a mount really as a shadow, youd have to be hosted by the creature, which is not riding), thief (and any skirmisher type rogue, tho always having an ally next to you means great things for sneak attack)... are the ones at a quick glance lose a lot of their class identity when a shadow.","created_at":"2021-03-10T10:01:39.494000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"819147988508475454","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"746818810954121236","content":"So back onto races, cause this conversation came up in mems on the other server....\n\nso d&d has 43 races + legacy, likely at least 3 more come ravenloft. we have 5 s3 races, and at least 4 s4 races.   thats 55 races\n\nwith the legacy options added in, thats 55 races that, based on ability scores are optimal for any class.  Add in varients and subraces, and thats massive bloat.\n\nI propose that we cull this list down a lot.  Focus on races we have had representation of, a few core one, and races that really fit the themes of Empire City.  even if we kept every variant and subrace of the remaining races, that should be plenty to choose from.  It would also encourage people to try out homebrew races that should be far more common.  Just a thought, but as we are moving to more and more of a custom setting, i think it would be an approprate step","created_at":"2021-03-10T17:23:35.542000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"819259204875190275","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"746818810954121236","content":"(dragonborn, dwarf, elf, gnome, half elf, human, goblin, kenku, tabaxi, kalashtar: this would be my core list of races that were either common last season (as i don't know s1 and s2 info really), or common enough in fantasy to belong.  I also would suggest more based on each zone, would have some specifically that would be approprate, like reborn and semic hybrid would be approprate for hampstead, but i wouldnt assume what would be approprate for others.  I left warforged off the list, as i feel scrap forged fill that niche)  anyway thats my thoughts, but it kinda would take a major consensus with the DMs to implement this level of restriction","created_at":"2021-03-10T17:30:16.133000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"819260885075099689","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
